    "body": "I think this reads a little ambiguously, and could be interpreted as \"it's been designed primarily for static relocations but nothing's stopping you using it for dynamic ones\" which is perhaps technically true but not the intended reading. Maybe something stronger like \"This scheme only specifies how to encode static relocations; a future version of this specification may extend the scheme to support dynamic relocations.\"?",
